    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42193" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">să_crĭfĭcŭlus</span></b> ,
			i, m.
		sacrifico, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>one who conducts the sacrifices</i>, <i>a sacrificer</i>, <i>sacrificing
				priest</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sacrificuli ac vates ceperant hominum mentes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					25, 1</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Suet. Dom. 1</span></i> (for which, sacricolae,
				<i><span class="en">Tac. H.
				3, 74</span></i>).—In apposition: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rex,</span>”
				<i>a high-priest</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					2, 2, 1</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">id. 6, 41, 9</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">v. rex, I.: vates,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					35, 48 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			</div>
